  "id": "Kingston-25_03243_FUL",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "(Retrospective) Change of use of an existing garden outbuilding to a small, part time beauty studio (Use Class E) for the provision of appointment only semi-permanent makeup treatments",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The limited period for the use hereby permitted shall be 5 years from the date of decision. On or before the expiration of this permission use as a beauty studio (Use Class E) shall be restored to its former use of residential outbuilding, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To accord with the application proposal and allow the local planning authority to test the development's impact on neighbouring amenity, in accordance with Policies DM10 and DM17 of the Council's LDF Core Strategy (April 2012).",
    "The outbuilding here permitted shall be occupied in the manner stated on the application form and ancillary to the occupation and enjoyment of the host property known as '58 Kingsmead Avenue Tolworth KT6 7PP' as a single dwelling. The outbuilding will not be used as a separate unit of accommodation or for any other business/employment purpose unless otherwise first agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: the establishment of an additional independent unit of accommodation would give rise to an over-intensive use of the site and lead to an unsatisfactory relationship between independent dwellings in conflict with policy DM10 (Design Requirements for New Developments including House Extensions) of the LDF Core Strategy Adopted April 2012.",
    "The premises to which this permission relates shall not be used for the purpose hereby permitted before 9am or after 6pm Monday to Saturday or at any time on Sundays or Bank Holidays\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "No advertisements shall be displayed on site without prior approval from the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
